आयातः सञ्चार ।

॰ सन्देशपरीक्षा — THE UDP AND DNS PROGRAM: a self-test, an echo server and client, a DNS
॰ responder and client (ADR-0048, milestone 3). Built with the eight library files beside it
॰ (spec/net/*.t1); tools/check-net-t1.sh and crates/yantra/tests/net_t1.rs build and run it.
॰
॰ ARGUMENTS, as spec/net/net-demo.t1 has them. With NONE the program runs the SELF-TEST and
॰ never touches a device. With one argument its first octet is the role:
॰   e   UDP echo server on 10.0.0.2 port 7: one datagram in, the same datagram back
॰   u   UDP client from 10.0.0.1 port 7001: send nine octets to 10.0.0.2 port 7, expect them back
॰   n   DNS responder on 10.0.0.2 port 53: answer one query with 192.0.2.7
॰   d   DNS client on 10.0.0.1: resolve "www.sas.test" against 10.0.0.2
॰   a   the DNS client of d with two more pairs on its allow-list: (10.0.0.9, 53) and (the server, 5353)
॰   b   a receiver on port 7 with a 20-octet buffer, listing (10.0.0.1, any) and (10.0.0.3, 99)
॰   q   DNS client on QEMU's user-mode network: 10.0.2.15 asks 10.0.2.3 for "localhost" (no WAIT)
॰
॰ OUTPUT. The self-test prints the UDP datagram (13 octets), the DNS query (30) and the DNS
॰ response (46) it builds, then one octet per check (94), '0' passing; it answers the number
॰ of checks that failed. A role prints "<letter> <status>" and a newline, the refusal's name
॰ after it when it is a ruled word, and a client that got an address prints "A <address>".
॰ The program leaves with the status, or for a refusal word its CODE.

सार्वजनिक चरः आदेशसङ्केतः ॱॱ न६४ भवति २४२८५२६६६०५९८२०३५ ।
